nt  calamity and disaster would follow  famine disease blight and murder  wherever he turned bad luck a misfortune  accompanied him it's very possible that  the worship of trona book was out of  fear family sacrificing cattle and given  everything they possessed to the God in  order to appease him and save them from  his cruelness and wrath chernobyl paints  this image of a God who thrives on pain  and suffering and almost takes pride in  bringing death for anyone who has seen  or read American Gods this is something  that you'll be quite familiar with as  here he describes death as an art form  boasting to have killed over 10,000  people and washing his hammer in the  blood of those he's slain now there are  some variations of Chernobyl  not seen as inherently evil and as we've  noticed of some mythologies and most  religions there is a tendency to fear  and must demonize any deity that has  some kind of association with death or  the underworld there's a scene in  American Gods where owner Bob describes  where he's from he says that everyone  there is the same color so they instead  argue over different shades of color  his brother Bela Bach had blond hair and  blue eyes so he was seen as the good one  whereas Chernabog had dark hair and dark  eyes meaning that he was naturally seen  as evil and so he became what everyone  expected of him some people have  attributed the battle between the two as  an explanation to the seasons when Bela  Bach was victorious he would bring  spring and summer and Chernobyl would  bring autumn and winter with winter does  come hardship illness and famine and  this could have contributed to the idea  that Chernabog was evil we can liken the  brothers to night and day with one  ruling over the dark portion of the year  and the other the brighter now whether  Chernabog was inherently evil or just  simply misunderstood is most likely a  question that we will never have the  answer to now for those of you wondering  about China books phys